  "body": "## What changed\n- add a dedicated market-statistics observer card above the normal Bots table\n- create/edit/delete the observer from a small credentials-only form (name, Vinted e-mail, password)\n- observer has no bot configuration, target, quota or negotiation steps\n- hide the observer from all regular bot repository reads so it cannot be started, edited or deleted through normal bot endpoints\n- keep the observer in the shared `bot` table only for encrypted credentials, a globally unique bot/session id, and safe session isolation\n\n## Automatic collector\n- remove the need for `FLIPBOT_MARKET_STATS_BOT_ID`\n- Playwright now resolves the currently configured observer through the backend\n- market-statistics collection is enabled by default and can be disabled with `FLIPBOT_MARKET_STATS_ENABLED=false`\n- first observer check occurs about 30 seconds after Playwright starts\n- if no observer exists, the collector stays idle and polls again; creating the observer in the frontend does not require changing the Run Configuration\n- successful full scans remain spaced by the configured interval (24h by default)\n- failures retry after 15 minutes without affecting normal bot workers\n\n## Isolation\n- the observer remains `STOPPED` in the normal bot domain and is never returned by normal `/api/bots` repository reads\n- normal RUNNING bots can operate at the same time as the observer collector\n- no real-offer, next-step, quota, persistent guard, or negotiation processor logic is changed",
